cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this data or code, please cite it as below."
type: dataset
title: "NLP-gestützte Erschließung von Metadaten in epigraphischen Datenbanken: Vokabular, Goldstandard und Methodenvergleich geprüft am Datensatz der Epigraphischen Datenbank Heidelberg (EDH)"
version: "1.0"
date-released: "2026-09-30"
authors:
  - family-names: Kilbinger
    given-names: Lisa
    affiliation: "Philipps-Universität Marburg"
license:
  - CC-BY-SA-4.0
  - MIT
abstract: >-
  A multilingual iconographic vocabulary (374 depicted elements, category tree,
  German/Latin/English search terms, 354 motif rules), aligned with Iconclass
  and the EAGLE vocabulary "Decoration"; a hand-annotated gold standard of
  1,100 randomly drawn comments of the Epigraphic Database Heidelberg (EDH),
  with a concordance to Trismegistos and EDCS; and a comparison of four
  methods (dictionary matching, lemmatisation, dependency parsing, fine-tuned
  BERT) that extract iconographic motifs from the free-text comments, with the
  complete code to reproduce all reported scores. Part of a PhD project on
  figurative decoration on Late Antique funerary inscriptions. Data in data/
  and figures/: CC BY-SA 4.0; code in src/: MIT.
keywords:
  - epigraphy
  - iconography
  - funerary inscriptions
  - Roman inscriptions
  - Late Antiquity
  - Early Christian art
  - Epigraphic Database Heidelberg
  - EDH
  - Iconclass
  - EAGLE
  - controlled vocabulary
  - gold standard
  - information extraction
  - natural language processing
  - BERT
  - digital art history
  - FAIR data
references:
  - type: database
    title: "Epigraphic Database Heidelberg (EDH)"
    url: "https://edh.ub.uni-heidelberg.de/"
    license: CC-BY-SA-4.0
  - type: database
